    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46796" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭperlātīvus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		superlatus; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in gram.: nomen,</span>”
				<i>superlative</i>, <i>in the superlative degree</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Charis. p. 87</span></i>
			 P.; <i><span class="en">Prisc. p. 605</span></i>
			ib.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Hyperbolic</i>, <i>exaggerated</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sententiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Isid. 2, 21, 16</span></i>
			. — Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭperlātīvē</span></b> ,
				<i>superlatively</i>, <i>in the
				superlative</i>, <i><span class="en">Charis. p. 87</span></i>
		P.</div>
